Since the flying backstab of doom is going away in the next version, how 
about applying a little constancy to the rules for backstab and twoweapon?

First of all make #twoweapon always take an action, to get in or out of 
it.  My reasoning for this is that alternative weapons are held in an 
easy carry fashion while wielded weapons are ready for use.

So an alternative spear is carried over your shoulder while twoweapon 
with two spears means that both points are forwards.  The grip differs 
and it takes time to change between the two modes.

The to-hit skill for a #twoweapon attack should be the least of the 
primary weapon skill, the secondary weapon skill and the twoweapon skill 
and any hit is credited to whichever of these skills has the lowest hit 
count that can be further advanced.  This gets rid of offhand unskilled 
silver sabres.

Next make it a consistent rule that backstabbing requires a melee strike 
with a weapon and a free hand.  So the character must be making a 
non-thrown strike with a one-handed weapon while not twoweaponing or 
wearing a shield.

Finally allow the backstab bonus against any unaware foe.  So if they 
are fleeing, asleep, peaceful (or tame), or just made a confused, 
stunned or displacement (or invisibility) distracted strike against the 
wrong target or empty space then they are open for a backstab.

-HJC


